# File: tests/features/routed-sessions.feature
# Generated from: specs/4-keep-routed-sessions-working-with-routed-compaction-subagents-and-auto-mode-permissions/requirements.md
Feature: Routed compaction, subagents and auto-mode permissions

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Compaction on a routed model uses its provider
    Given "opencode-go/glm-5.1" is selected
    When the user runs "/compact keep the plan"
    Then the summary comes from OpenCode Go with "keep the plan" in its request, the conversation becomes one summary message, and no request goes to Anthropic

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Reaching the threshold summarizes in place on the provider
    Given a routed model with a 128000-token context window
    When a main-loop turn ends with 108800 routed context tokens
    Then the mod summarizes on the provider, the next routed request carries the summary and only the newer messages, and nothing is sent to Anthropic

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Subagents are answered by their own model and hand back their report
    Given a Claude main loop with a subagent on "opencode-go/glm-5.3", and a routed main loop with a Claude subagent
    When each subagent's steps fire
    Then the routed subagent uses its own transcript and model and delivers its report through SubagentHandback, and the Claude subagent passes through

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Default permission mode follows first-party login presence
    Given the routed auto-mode permissions row is unset
    When the session has, or lacks, a first-party Anthropic login
    Then the effective mode is "claude-classifier", or "server-classifier-off", and the mod loads

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Claude classifier decides routed Bash calls
    Given mode "claude-classifier" and auto mode on
    When a routed Bash call reaches tool.check with no rule settling it
    Then the classifier's allow or deny is the decision, and an ask or a failed classification is put to the person

  @SCN006
  Scenario: The person decides routed calls the classifier can't
    Given mode "server-classifier-off" and auto mode on
    When a routed Bash call needs a verdict
    Then nmg-router asks the person, Allow runs the call and Deny refuses it, and no missing server verdict blocks it

  @SCN007
  Scenario: Rules and Claude calls keep their verdicts
    Given either mode
    When a call matches an allow or deny rule, or comes from a Claude model
    Then Claude Code's own verdict is returned unchanged

  @SCN008
  Scenario: A failed in-place summary does not fall back to Claude
    Given a routed main loop at its threshold
    When the provider fails while summarizing in place
    Then one line names the provider, the provider's view is unchanged, the summary is retried at the next turn end, and no request goes to Anthropic
